2. THE FOUR NORMS

2.1 The Norm Set

A9 targets four certification norms:

Norm Domain Level Scheme
ISO 26262 Automotive functional safety ASIL A–D
IEC 61508 Industrial functional safety SIL 1–4
DO-178C / ED-12C Aerospace software DAL A–E
IEC 62443 Industrial cybersecurity SL 1–4

These are the four norms referenced by A0 and by the ST-T1024 & The 4 Norms position paper.

2.2 Why These Four

They share a common technical foundation (determinism, traceability, isolation, immutability, fail-safe behavior, verifiability) — see the position paper §2. They are the norms that matter for the domains where agentic ST-T1024 has the most immediate application: automotive, industrial, aerospace, and critical infrastructure.

2.3 What Certification Under Each Norm Requires

Each norm defines a process and a dossier. The process differs by norm; the dossier structure is similar.

Norm Dossier Name Key Artifacts
ISO 26262 Safety Case Item Definition, HARA, FMEDA, Safety Plan, Safety Case Report
IEC 61508 Safety Manual Safety Requirements Spec, Architecture Design, Verification Plan, FMEDA
DO-178C Software Accomplishment Summary PSAC, SDP, SVP, SCI, SAS
IEC 62443 Security Assurance Case Zones & Conduits, Risk Assessment, SL Target, Security Requirements

A9 does not reproduce these documents. A9 specifies which ST-T1024 artifacts fill which sections.

