3.4 The Verification Chain Theorem

Proposition A9-V (Chain Soundness). Certification is possible if and only if all three layers are complete and consistent.

Proof.

· Necessity. A certification dossier must cite evidence. Evidence comes from completed artifacts. If any layer is incomplete, the corresponding evidence is missing.
· Sufficiency. If all three layers are complete, each certification requirement maps to a specific artifact (by the traceability matrix of §4). The dossier is complete.

□

Corollary A9-V1. Certification cannot be pursued before Layer 3 is complete.

Corollary A9-V2. Layer 2 is a prerequisite for Layer 3 — hardware validation requires a machine-checked model against which the hardware is compared.

