10. OPEN DESIGN TENSIONS

# Question Impact
1 Gap classification. What counts as a "gap"? Is a deployment-specific artifact a gap, or a downstream obligation? Affects readiness criteria.
2 Norm-specific dossier differences. The four norms have different dossier formats. Does A9 need four separate dossier specs? May require sub-specs.
3 Independent review criteria. Who qualifies as "independent"? What are their credentials? Regulatory question.
4 Cross-norm artifact reuse. Which artifacts are shared across norms? Efficiency opportunity.
5 TLAPS necessity. Is TLAPS required for all norms, or only for DAL A / ASIL D? Affects timeline.
6 Hardware variance. Different hardware targets (DSP, RISC-V, ASIC) may have different certification implications. Per-target sub-dossiers.
7 Version control for the dossier. How does the dossier evolve when A1–A8 are updated? Configuration management.
8 Submission cadence. One norm at a time, or parallel submissions? Sequential recommended, but parallel may be faster if artifacts allow.

None are fatal. All must be resolved before pursuing certification.

